# ServiceRadar v1.3.4

Ingestion-pipeline scale and reliability hardening: a complete EventWriter
flow-control overhaul, vulnerability advisory feeds moved into core, endpoint
software inventory deltas, and a broad sweep of observability, capacity,
identity, and add-on regression fixes.

## Whats New

**1.3.4**
- Fixed the EventWriter ingestion pipeline that could exhaust core memory under
  even a small fleet: bounded JetStream consumer flow control (server-enforced
  max-ack-pending plus a producer overflow NAK), a rule-sharded stateful alert
  engine so disjoint alert rules evaluate in parallel instead of serializing
  through a single GenServer, and a per-device correlation cache so events
  resolve their device once per device instead of a synchronous DB query per
  event — eliminating an unbounded refc-binary leak and the resulting OOM/crash
  cascade.
- Moved vulnerability advisory feed ingestion (CISA KEV, VulnCheck KEV, VulnCheck
  nist-nvd2, NVD CVE 2.0) out of the agent add-on and into core-elx as
  disk-staged, AshOban-scheduled workers with hybrid JSONB plus indexed
  coordinate storage and a CPE-component, version-range endpoint matcher; retired
  the advisory-producer add-on.
- Hardened endpoint software inventory: change-gated (~hourly) uploads with
  package-set deltas, fixed the osv-scalibr nil-panic, corrected inventory
  directory ownership so periodic scans keep uploading, enabled scans for
  assigned agents, and stopped partial or unchanged uploads from wiping a full
  inventory.
- Fixed capacity forecasting regressions: bounded exhaustion projections (no more
  far-future or past-dated exhaustion), SNMP counter-reset contamination
  rejection, and empty-series persistence.
- web-ng: add-on fleet reporting (agent x add-on x version/hash/state), paginated
  and searchable endpoint package and device process tables, a package detail
  modal with vulnerability matches, restored sysmon process-metrics visibility,
  software-tab gating, and pre-populated vulnerability-feed URLs.
- Fixed add-on profile reconciliation (a return-type crash and a create-only
  agent_uid update error) and added a periodic auto-reconcile job so profile
  target queries (e.g. in:devices) materialize add-on assignments automatically.
- Observability: resolved traces that rendered without a service or operation
  name via an orphan-trace root fallback, and recreate JetStream durables on
  filter-subject drift.
- Device identity (DIRE): reciprocal agent_id anchoring and stale agent-device
  mislink repair with a distinct-hardware merge guard.
- Agent config delivery: one deferred config section no longer blocks the rest of
  the apply, redundant re-applies on an unchanged config version are skipped,
  add-on systemd units that go missing self-heal, and the version ldflag is
  corrected so released agents report their real version.
- Demo reliability: persisted agent-gateway (3Gi) and core-elx (16Gi) memory
  limits in the chart to stop OOM restarts.

